              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "enhanced_pre_training_named",
            "text": "The conclusion names \"enhanced BERT pre-training\" as one of the three main technologies introduced to improve performance, alongside soft label embedding and NER pre-training.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "paper_id": "1908.05908",
                "chunk_id": "c-0f3bf35195202e464e2739cc"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "crf_on_bert",
            "text": "For the named entity recognition task, a linear-chain CRF is built on top of BERT, with the score function being BERT's output at each character.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "paper_id": "1908.05908",
                "chunk_id": "c-7d1d8e2a3018e917195e868c"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "ner_pretraining_corpus",
            "text": "A large-scale Baidu Baike corpus is introduced for entity recognition pre-training, which is weakly supervised since there are no actual named entity labels.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "paper_id": "1908.05908",
                "chunk_id": "c-59affd016a6cbaeed876468f"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "soft_label_embedding",
            "text": "Soft label embedding is proposed to effectively transmit information between entity recognition and relation extraction.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "paper_id": "1908.05908",
                "chunk_id": "c-59affd016a6cbaeed876468f"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "multihead_relation_prediction",
            "text": "Relation classification is formulated as multi-head selection, and a multi-sigmoid layer is used for relation prediction since the same entity pair may have multiple relations, with cross-entropy loss minimized during training.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "paper_id": "1908.05908",
                "chunk_id": "c-3fd51d54d4cee4f5bef3a97a"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "single_model_f1",
            "text": "With a single model, the approach achieves an F1-score of 0.876 on testset-1.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "paper_id": "1908.05908",
                "chunk_id": "c-59affd016a6cbaeed876468f"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "ensemble_f1",
            "text": "By ensembling four variants of the model, the paper reports F1 score 0.892 (1st place) on testset-1 and F1 score 0.8924 (2nd place) on testset-2.",
